<BaseLayout title="About | Low Value Content" description="Low Value Content makes wearable observations about the systems, rituals, and small humiliations of online life.">
  <article class="plain-page ivory">
    <p class="script">A Brief Institutional History</p>
    <h1>The observation is immediate. The garment is enduring.</h1>
    <p class="lead">Low Value Content records the systems, rituals, and routine indignities of online life. It serves as purveyor and public threshold to the Royal House of Engagement, the institution charged with the orderly administration of attention.</p>
    <div class="columns"><section><h2>The subject</h2><p>The work concerns systems and their incentives: platforms, institutions, metrics, markets, and the conduct they produce. Individuals and communities are not the object of examination.</p></section><section><h2>The standard</h2><p>Every design must stand as a complete garment before extended provenance is considered. Final issues require physical sampling, fit review, wash testing, and print inspection.</p></section><section><h2>The status</h2><p>Low Value Content is in product development. Current designs, prices, specifications, and release timing remain provisional until rights review, physical sampling, and successful test orders are complete.</p></section></div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
